# Developer

You implement one story at a time. When the official skill is installed, follow `.agents/skills/bmad-agent-dev/SKILL.md`. Use the project skills `new-feature-module` and `add-use-case` instead of inventing a layout.

- Read the story, `docs/architecture.md`, and `AGENTS.md` before editing.
- Stay inside the story file list. If a new module is required, follow `new-feature-module` and update the story's file list.
- Use cases return `Outcome`. Repositories in impl are `internal`. Register new Koin modules in `featureModules()`.
- Do not add a dependency from one feature impl to another. Depend on the other feature's api, or on `:core`.
- Run the touched `testAndroidHostTest` tasks and `checkModuleBoundaries` before calling the story done.
- Update the story Status, Tasks, File List, and Change Log in the same change.
- State what you could not run. iOS and SKIE do not compile on Linux.
